0	# Sprint 15 — Modern Dashboard Redesign Spec
1	
2	**Author:** Vega | **Date:** 2026-04-15 | **Status:** READY FOR KODA
3	
4	---
5	
6	## Root Cause Analysis
7	
8	The scaffold look has one structural cause repeated across the entire app:
9	
10	- `--color-background` and `--color-card` are both `oklch(99% 0 0)` — cards are invisible against the page
11	- The sidebar at `oklch(97%)` is barely distinguishable from the main canvas
12	- There is NO `.dark` block for the semantic palette — dark mode falls back to light mode tokens
13	- `--shadow-card` is too subtle at `oklch(10% 0 0 / 0.08)` on a near-white surface
14	- The page background provides zero context — it reads as a blank document, not a product
15	
16	Fix: differentiate `background` from `card`, give the page a warm off-white, give cards a pure white surface with a real border, and add a proper dark mode block. That single change transforms every page instantly.
17	
18	---
19	
20	## Decision: Light Mode Default
21	
22	Light mode is the correct default for InkOS. Tattoo studio owners read this between clients in bright studio lighting. DaySmart, Phorest, and TSP are all light. Dark mode exists as an option (theme toggle already in header) but should not be the default or the focus of design effort.
23	
24	---
25	
26	## 1. Token Changes — `app/globals.css`
27	
28	These are surgical replacements inside the existing `@theme inline` block. Do NOT touch any specialty tokens (consent, calendar, booking-flow, artist colors). Only replace the semantic palette block and add the missing dark block.
29	
30	### Replace the SEMANTIC PALETTE block (lines 13–40 in current globals.css)
31	
32	```css
33	/* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
34	   SEMANTIC PALETTE — LIGHT MODE
35	────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
36	
37	/* Page canvas — warm off-white so cards "float" on it */
38	--color-background: oklch(97.5% 0.003 264);
39	
40	/* Text — near-black with a cool blue tint */
41	--color-foreground: oklch(13% 0.015 264);
42	
43	/* Card surface — pure white, visible against the page bg */
44	--color-card: oklch(100% 0 0);
45	--color-card-foreground: oklch(13% 0.015 264);
46	
47	--color-popover: oklch(100% 0 0);
48	--color-popover-foreground: oklch(13% 0.015 264);
49	
50	/* Primary — same purple, unchanged */
51	--color-primary: oklch(52% 0.24 292);
52	--color-primary-foreground: oklch(99% 0 0);
53	
54	/* Secondary — subtle lavender tint */
55	--color-secondary: oklch(95.5% 0.012 292);
56	--color-secondary-foreground: oklch(28% 0.06 292);
57	
58	/* Muted — for backgrounds of non-interactive elements */
59	--color-muted: oklch(95% 0.006 264);
60	--color-muted-foreground: oklch(52% 0.02 264);
61	
62	/* Accent — light purple for hover states and chips */
63	--color-accent: oklch(95% 0.018 292);
64	--color-accent-foreground: oklch(35% 0.14 292);
65	
66	/* Destructive — unchanged */
67	--color-destructive: oklch(59% 0.22 27);
68	--color-destructive-foreground: oklch(99% 0 0);
69	
70	/* Borders — visible but light */
71	--color-border: oklch(91% 0.008 264);
72	--color-input: oklch(91% 0.008 264);
73	--color-ring: oklch(52% 0.24 292);
74	```
75	
76	### Replace the SHADOWS block
77	
78	```css
79	/* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
80	   SHADOWS — custom (never use Tailwind default shadow-sm/md)
81	────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
82	
83	/* Soft border shadow for cards on white */
84	--shadow-soft: 0 1px 2px 0 oklch(13% 0.015 264 / 0.05), 0 1px 3px 0 oklch(13% 0.015 264 / 0.04);
85	
86	/* Standard card elevation — visible on off-white page */
87	--shadow-card: 0 1px 3px 0 oklch(13% 0.015 264 / 0.07), 0 1px 2px -1px oklch(13% 0.015 264 / 0.05);
88	
89	/* Hover elevation */
90	--shadow-card-hover: 0 4px 12px -2px oklch(13% 0.015 264 / 0.10), 0 2px 6px -2px oklch(13% 0.015 264 / 0.07);
91	
92	/* Medium depth for drawers, modals */
93	--shadow-soft-md: 0 4px 16px -4px oklch(13% 0.015 264 / 0.10), 0 2px 8px -2px oklch(13% 0.015 264 / 0.07);
94	```
95	
